  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "A.Selvam vs The Food Safety Officer on 24 April, 2024 Crl.O.P.(MD) Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 24.04.2024 Coram: The Hon'Ble Mr Justice A.A.Nakkiran Crl.O.P.(MD)No.18127 of 2022 and Crl.MP(MD)Nos.12124 & 12126 of 2022 A.Selvam ... Petitioner / Accused No.1 Vs. The Food Safety Officer, Code No.109 & 120, Chellampatti & Vadipatti Taluk, Designated Officers Office, Multipurpose Health Supervisors (F) Training School, Viswanathapuram, Madurai 625 014. ... Respondent / Complainant Prayer: Criminal Original Petition is filed under Section 482 Cr.P.C for the records and quash the proceedings in S.T.C.No.9 of 2022 on of the learned Judicial Magistrate, Vadipatti, insofar as the petit concerned. For Petitioner : Mr.M.Rajaraman For Respondent : Mr.K.Sanjai Gandhi, Government Advocate (Crl.Side) 1/6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O. Order A.Selvam vs The Food Safety Officer on 24 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/107853140/ 1 2. As per Rule 2.4.6(1) and Section 46(4) of the https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O.P.(MD)No.18127 of 2022 Food Safety and Standards Act, the appeal has to be filed before A.Selvam vs The Food Safety Officer on 24 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/107853140/ 2 within 30 days.",
    "facts": "The Food Analyst had sent a report on 28.09.2020 stating that the sample was substandard. The petitioner filed an appeal before the Designated Officer under Section 46(4) of the Food Safety and Standards Act in Form VII. But, in this case, the Designated Officer had not disposed this appeal and also not forwarded the one part of the sample to the referral laboratory and thus, violated the Food Safety and Standards Act as per Rules 2.4.6. The Food Analyst had sent a report on 28.09.2020 stating that the sample was substandard. Thereafter, the Designated Officer had sent the report of the Food Analyst along with his notice, dated 14.10.2020. After receiving the report, the petitioner filed an appeal before the Designated Officer under Rule 2.4.6(1) and Section 46(4) of the Food Safety and Standards Act.",
    "arguments": "3. The learned Additional Public Prosecutor appearing for the respondent submitted that the petitioner ought to have filed an appeal to the Designated Officer in Form -VIII instead of Form VII and hence, he objected to quash the proceedings."
  },
